---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import exposure from '../data/shodan.json';
---
<Layout title="Shodan Exposure Intelligence | CyberIntel"><div class="shell"><section class="hero"><span class="tag">EXTERNAL EXPOSURE RESEARCH</span><h1>Shodan <span class="accent">Intelligence</span></h1><p>Aggregated observations about indexed internet-facing services. This section is intentionally public-summary-only: no API keys, host-by-host vulnerable target lists or unauthorised scans.</p></section><section class="stats"><div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Research query</div><strong style="font-size:21px">{exposure.query ?? 'Not configured'}</strong><small>Configure a permitted aggregate query in the workflow</small></div><div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Indexed observations</div><strong>{exposure.total === null ? '—' : exposure.total.toLocaleString('en-GB')}</strong><small>Shodan index observations; not confirmed vulnerabilities</small></div><div class="stat"><div class="eyebrow">Last fetched</div><strong style="font-size:18px">{exposure.updated_at ?? 'Not yet synced'}</strong><small>Dependent on API access and rate limits</small></div></section><section class="section"><div class="card"><h3>Connecting Shodan safely</h3><p>Set <code>SHODAN_API_KEY</code> in GitHub Actions secrets and configure a non-sensitive aggregate query as <code>SHODAN_QUERY</code> in repository variables. Run the provided Python enrichment script. Query-count access varies by subscription; never put your API key in frontend code.</p><p>API docs: <a class="accent" href="https://developer.shodan.io/api">developer.shodan.io/api →</a></p></div></section></div></Layout>
